# In insert mode (IRM), a character printed on one line of a
# double-height pair moves only that line's text, up to the line's last
# column, column 5 of 10. The other line of the pair keeps its text, so
# the two halves of the doubled characters no longer match.
# spec: the VT100 User Guide, DECDHL: "The use of double-width characters reduces the number of characters per line by half"; "the same character output must be sent to both lines to form full double-height characters"; the VT510 manual, IRM: "If IRM mode is set, then new characters move characters in page memory to the right. Characters moved past the page's right border are lost"
# covers: ANSI-4, text.line-size
size 10 3
send "\e#3abcde\r\n\e#4abcde\e[1;2H\e[4hX"
dump
send "\e[2;3HYZ"
dump
